---

# Synthetic Data Rules

The data should model realistic telecom behaviour.

Relationships must exist.

Examples:

Urban customers use more mobile data.

Rural customers use more voice.

Students buy smaller data bundles.

SMEs use more mobile money.

Recharge frequency influences churn.

Campaign targeting influences response.

December has higher activity.

January slows after holidays.

Data revenue grows over time.

Voice revenue slowly declines.

Do not generate unrelated random columns.

---

# Customer Lifecycle

Active

Activity within 30 days.

At Risk

31–45 inactive days.

Dormant

46–59 inactive days.

Churned

60+ inactive days.

Reactivated

Activity after churn.

Lifecycle must be derived from generated activity.

---

# Executive Recommendation Rules

Recommendations must never be random.

Each recommendation requires:

Finding

Supporting KPI

Business Impact

Recommended Action

Priority

Responsible Department

Recommendations must always be supported by metrics.

---

# Dashboard Rules

Every dashboard page must include:

KPI Summary

Trend Analysis

Regional or Segment Comparison

Business Finding

Business Impact

Recommended Action

Avoid creating pages that only contain charts.

---

# Streamlit Rules

Streamlit pages should only:

Load data

Call analytics services

Display charts

Display recommendations

No KPI calculations inside page files.

---

# Testing

Every business calculation must have tests.

Every KPI must be reproducible.

Validate:

Dates

Ranges

Duplicates

Relationships

Referential Integrity

Schema

Business Rules

---

# Git Workflow

One commit per completed phase.

After each phase commit, push to the remote:

git push -u origin HEAD

Commit messages:

feat:

fix:

docs:

test:

perf:

refactor:

chore:

Never mix unrelated changes.

---

# Cursor Behaviour

When implementing work:

Inspect before editing.

Never overwrite files without checking.

Explain assumptions.

Prefer reusable code.

Stop after completing the requested phase.

Never continue automatically.
